# HR Insight AI — Audit Logs Endpoint
# Requires: REST Client VS Code extension
# Backend runs on port 3010 (npm run start:dev)
#
# Workflow:
# 1. Open auth.http → run TEST 4 (admin login) → copy token → paste into @adminToken
# 2. Open auth.http → run TEST 2 (viewer login) → copy token → paste into @viewerToken
# 3. Run tests below in order — some tests depend on data created by previous ones

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3010
@contentType = application/json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️  NO quotes — paste raw token strings only
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
@adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE
@viewerToken = PASTE_VIEWER_TOKEN_HERE
@hrToken = PASTE_HR_MANAGER_TOKEN_HERE

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paste a user UUID after running TEST 4 in users.http
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
@someUserId = PASTE_ANY_USER_UUID_HERE


### ❌ TEST 1 — Get audit logs WITHOUT token (should return 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs


### ❌ TEST 2 — Get audit logs with VIEWER token (should return 403 Forbidden)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}


### ✅ TEST 3 — Get ALL audit logs with ADMIN token (should return 200 + paginated data)
# This returns all audit entries — check that meta.total > 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 4 — Get audit logs with HR_MANAGER token (should also return 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{hrToken}}


### ✅ TEST 5 — Filter by action: CREATE only
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?action=CREATE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 6 — Filter by action: DELETE only
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?action=DELETE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 7 — Filter by action: UPDATE only
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?action=UPDATE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 8 — Filter by specific userId
# Paste an admin user UUID to see only their actions
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?userId={{someUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 9 — Filter by entityType: USER
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?entityType=USER
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 10 — Filter by entityType: TEAM
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?entityType=TEAM
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 11 — Filter by date range (today only)
# Replace the date with today's date in ISO format
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?from=2026-02-27T00:00:00Z&to=2026-02-27T23:59:59Z
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 12 — Pagination: page 1, 5 items per page
# Check meta.totalPages — if total > 5, should be > 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?page=1&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 13 — Pagination: page 2, 5 items per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?page=2&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ✅ TEST 14 — Combined filters: CREATE actions for USER entity
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?action=CREATE&entityType=USER
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### GENERATE AUDIT DATA — Run these to create entries, then re-run TEST 3 above
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### ✅ GENERATE 1 — Register a new user (creates a CREATE/USER audit entry)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "audit.test@example.com",
  "password": "AuditTest123!",
  "firstName": "Audit",
  "lastName": "Test"
}


### ✅ GENERATE 2 — Change a user's role (creates an UPDATE/USER audit entry)
# Replace :id with a real user UUID from TEST 3 in users.http
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{someUserId}}/role
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "role": "HR_MANAGER"
}
